{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition","id":1501066,"title":"Long-time Player, New to Exalted 3rd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-22T14:59:20-08:00","id":1501066,"title":"Long-time Player, New to Exalted 3rd Edition","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I've been playing Exalted since the 1st edition core but I never got a chance to reallly play ex3 until about 6 months or so ago. Since then, I've had a lot of issues with the Solar charm set. I've rewritten a lot of it (basically just condensing the bloat) but a lot of it just seems awful. For instance, an I missing something or is Melee just hands down the best defensive tree even though it also is the arguably the best offensive tree as well.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of questions so I figured I'd ask them in my own thread so not to bug the devs (who seem to be busy now) or fill the forum with one question at a time.<br /> <br /> First question: By my reading of Reflex Sidestep Technique, this is the only way to get &quot;access&quot; to your dodge charms during an ambush as the ambush renders your def inapplicable. Therefore, you can't apply dodge charms to the ambush as you can't apply your Evasion. This would make 7SE inapplicable even though it is trying really hard to be applicable. <br /> <br /> But, for some reason HGD can bypass ambushes for 4m? <br /> <br /> So, which is it? Can I use 7SE on ambushes or can't I? If I can't, why is HGD the greatest charm in the book?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T17:28:54-08:00","id":1501081,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel any better, after a year of fighting with E3, my table just went back to E1. I am kinda hoping Essence works better for us, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T00:59:16-08:00","id":1501378,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>HGD is weaker in the scenario where you don't have enough initiative to buy off the damage successes. So it isn't great right after resetting to base initiative, for example, when non-Dawns only have a couple of initiative to buy off damage or hit crash.</li> <li>Even if you do have the initiative, particularly devastating attacks with 10ish or whatever successes would be very expensive to buy off with HGD, but the same flat cost for 7SE.</li> <li>HGD can't be used at all in crash, as it is Perilous, while 7SE can.</li> <li>Technically, HGD can't be activated in response to Withering attacks, while 7SE could be. Of course, I'd be wary of blowing a once-per-scene perfect defense against a withering attack, but it's theoretically an option...</li> </ol>That said, assuming that you have the initiative to buy off the attack successes, yes, I would agree that HGD is the stronger charm, especially since I don't think I ever saw 7SE get successfully reset. But as you've already mentioned, Dodge has another Charm dedicated to ambushes, so a serious Dodge-er has the option to buy both.<br /> <br /> I would also second Asmodai's suggestion that if you've struggled this long with 3E and it still isn't working for you, you should at least consider going back to another edition or waiting in the hope for Essence to work out better. I tried for a very long time to hammer 3E into a shape that my group could enjoy and it was a pretty thankless task compared the relative simplicity of reverting to another ruleset that worked better for us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T03:20:05-08:00","id":1501390,"title":"","content":"I don't think ambushes are necessarily something you need a hard answer to.<br /> The main time surprise attacks get upgraded to ambushes without specific charms is when you've not only failed to spot the unseen enemy but also lost a join battle roll and well, that's normally a sign of bigger problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T03:53:00-08:00","id":1501394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501390#post1501390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think ambushes are necessarily something you need a hard answer to.<br /> The main time surprise attacks get upgraded to ambushes without specific charms is when you've not only failed to spot the unseen enemy but also lost a join battle roll and well, that's normally a sign of bigger problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that both Join Battle and opposing Stealth are rolls for the same ability, most characters with an Awareness of 0 or 1 are probably going to be beaten by a stealth guy in both of them. Of the QC mortals, even the conscript has 5 in both Stealth and Join Battle, more than enough to beat many low Awareness PCs reliably - and that's by the guy with the concept of &quot;I just got handed a spear for the first time&quot;, not &quot;pro assassin&quot; or even &quot;experienced bandit&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, it isn't as likely to be lethal in 3E, since combat is really hard to resolve with one damage roll, even if it's unopposed.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd prioritize maxing out Awareness before worrying about anti-ambush Charms, but that's before you start considering actual assassins - Stealth 9, Join Battle 7, which can be rough for a lot of PCs to beat at either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-26-2023, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T07:23:09-08:00","id":1501402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501394#post1501394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that both Join Battle and opposing Stealth are rolls for the same ability, most characters with an Awareness of 0 or 1 are probably going to be beaten by a stealth guy in both of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the typical game experience is that you'll be with a circle with other player characters who presumably will at least have a fighting character with at least peak mortal reflexes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-26-2023, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T19:10:34-08:00","id":1501445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition#post1501066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I've been playing Exalted since the 1st edition core but I never got a chance to reallly play ex3 until about 6 months or so ago. Since then, I've had a lot of issues with the Solar charm set. I've rewritten a lot of it (basically just condensing the bloat) but a lot of it just seems awful. For instance, an I missing something or is Melee just hands down the best defensive tree even though it also is the arguably the best offensive tree as well.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>Melee always seemed if not as good better than dodge for defence in those prior editions too I found?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T12:00:46-08:00","id":1501556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501378#post1501378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>HGD is weaker in the scenario where you don't have enough initiative to buy off the damage successes. So it isn't great right after resetting to base initiative, for example, when non-Dawns only have a couple of initiative to buy off damage or hit crash.</li> <li>Even if you do have the initiative, particularly devastating attacks with 10ish or whatever successes would be very expensive to buy off with HGD, but the same flat cost for 7SE.</li> <li>HGD can't be used at all in crash, as it is Perilous, while 7SE can.</li> <li>Technically, HGD can't be activated in response to Withering attacks, while 7SE could be. Of course, I'd be wary of blowing a once-per-scene perfect defense against a withering attack, but it's theoretically an option...</li> </ol>That said, assuming that you have the initiative to buy off the attack successes, yes, I would agree that HGD is the stronger charm, especially since I don't think I ever saw 7SE get successfully reset. But as you've already mentioned, Dodge has another Charm dedicated to ambushes, so a serious Dodge-er has the option to buy both.<br /> <br /> I would also second Asmodai's suggestion that if you've struggled this long with 3E and it still isn't working for you, you should at least consider going back to another edition or waiting in the hope for Essence to work out better. I tried for a very long time to hammer 3E into a shape that my group could enjoy and it was a pretty thankless task compared the relative simplicity of reverting to another ruleset that worked better for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all valid weaknesses to HGD but yeah I think my main gripe is that it acts like three separate Dodge charms (Reflex Sidestep, 7SE, and Vaporous Division) in one Melee charm. IMO that should be reversed as dodge is way more specific in its application. Also, it seems that the common equation to the Solar charms is that 1 initiative = 4m, as in the difference in costs of VD and HGD. Does this seem balanced? I changed the cost to 3m in VD and have not seen any abuse yet. The reason I bring this up is that Reed in the Wind costs 2 init for every 1m in comparison to an excellency so why does the VD cost 8 times more than HGD for the same effect (4m to 1init)? Am I mathing wrong on that?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 01-28-2023, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T12:05:50-08:00","id":1501557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501445#post1501445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Melee always seemed if not as good better than dodge for defence in those prior editions too I found?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but at least in 2nd edition you could add your essence to your dodge score. Also, it seems like almost every effect in the book is undodgeable but easily blockable in this edition for some reason. Multiple spells and Charms have this listing for no reason. I'm pretty sure it's easier to dodge behind a rock against Cascade of Cutting Terror than it is to samurai slash dozens of blades coming at you but according to Holden and Morke, that's a no. I don't get why this edition seems to be hellbent on making dodge awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T12:11:58-08:00","id":1501558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501390#post1501390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think ambushes are necessarily something you need a hard answer to.<br /> The main time surprise attacks get upgraded to ambushes without specific charms is when you've not only failed to spot the unseen enemy but also lost a join battle roll and well, that's normally a sign of bigger problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'm not misreading Ambushes then, correct? It's pretty terribly spelled out but by saying your defense is set to 0, that means that you can't apply defensive charms as well? Because the only place I've seen that backed up is in Reflex Sidestep. And the only place that straight up says it can be used against ambushes is RST and HGD, and HGD works automatically while RST is a bitch to get to work (especially the higher your Evasion score which also makes ZERO sense, but oh well). <br /> <br /> So you'd have to somehow get your Evasion back to 5 (I'm assuming if you give a shit about dodge you'd be there) just to use 7SE, but HGD is just an easy 4m which completely renders ambush builds pointless btw. Once again, for some reason Dodge seems to get the shaft even though it should be better at getting out of the way of such things. <br /> <br /> I guess the only thing that would stop it is if you attacked an HGD guy while his sword was sheathed? Would that work?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T02:27:03-08:00","id":1501599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501556#post1501556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are all valid weaknesses to HGD but yeah I think my main gripe is that it acts like three separate Dodge charms (Reflex Sidestep, 7SE, and Vaporous Division) in one Melee charm. IMO that should be reversed as dodge is way more specific in its application. Also, it seems that the common equation to the Solar charms is that 1 initiative = 4m, as in the difference in costs of VD and HGD. Does this seem balanced? I changed the cost to 3m in VD and have not seen any abuse yet. The reason I bring this up is that Reed in the Wind costs 2 init for every 1m in comparison to an excellency so why does the VD cost 8 times more than HGD for the same effect (4m to 1init)? Am I mathing wrong on that?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>You are indeed mathing wrong. Partially because you are doing at least one math thing wrong, but far more importantly, because you assume the designers were considering mote/initiative efficiency exchange rate when writing Charms.<br /> <br /> You can spend 2m on an Excellency to raise a static value like DV by 1. By the basic application of Reed, spending 2i increases Evasion by 1. So, in this case, 1 initiative is worth a little more than 1 mote, as activating Reed also raises the cap on your potential DV by your Essence - a potential benefit, but I don't think it's enough to radically alter efficiency for this discussion. Let's call it 1:1.<br /> <br /> Next, HGD isn't just an initiative cost for the damage cancelling effect - it's 4 motes flat cost plus 1 initiative per damage cancelled. Because part of HGD's cost is variable and part is flat, it's impossible to set a simple mote to initiative cost between HGD and VD - VD is 1i cheaper at 1 blocked success, then VD is paying 4 motes for 2i, then 8 motes for 3i, 12 motes for 4i... by those conversions, 1i starts at literally worthless at 1i=0, and attempts to reach 1i to 4m, but will never quite get there because math.<br /> <br /> So, we have 1i=1m, 1i=0, 1i=2m, and 1i is slightly under 4m, derived from looking at just a few Charms. I'm sure we can find other exchange rates given even a little bit of effort, but I think that proves the point.<br /> <br /> In other words, as far as I can tell, there isn't any balanced conversion cost between initiative and motes. Trying to assign one is just going to drive you crazy because you're assuming that sort of thing was being carefully considered during design, but if it was, it isn't really well reflected in the final product.<br /> <br /> Math aside, I'd say that I think Dodge Charms overall should be better. Dodge has always felt underwhelming to me. It's theoretically valuable as a Charm tree that punishes attackers by draining their initiative and sucking it up for your use, but in a game with transparent mechanics where attackers know that's going to happen after they've taken a first swing, most opponents are just going to attack any other available targets and the Dodge Supernal is just going to sit there and not get attacked. If you're focusing on Dodge as your primary combat ability, you definitely still need a good offensive ability that will force your opponent to consider you a threat... that said, this has always been the case in Exalted, so it isn't really anything new.<br /> <br /> At least part of your specific problem at the moment seems to be that HGD is a weird, badly written, badly balanced Charm with too many different benefits for different costs. It's been referred to as &quot;Word Soup&quot; in another now-ancient thread on the subject, and I think there's good reason for that. If you think it's trying to act like 3 different Charms, I'd suggest that the easiest fix would be to cut it up into three different Charms.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 01-29-2023, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T04:55:01-08:00","id":1501603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501558#post1501558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the only thing that would stop it is if you attacked an HGD guy while his sword was sheathed? Would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me the important question is who's the player character in this situation.<br /> <br /> It's reasonable to say a character can't employ a defensive melee charm when they don't have a melee weapon. It's my opinion that HGD mentioning unexpected attacks was future proofing against magic that gives attacks the properties of an ambush rather than allow a Solar being able to parry an assassin's dagger while asleep in their bed despite their sword being all the way across the room.<br /> <br /> However, people are substantially less reasonable when it's their character on the line and they can't technically defend themselves because their sword is on their hip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-04-2023, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T07:54:39-08:00","id":1501611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501599#post1501599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are indeed mathing wrong. Partially because you are doing at least one math thing wrong, but far more importantly, because you assume the designers were considering mote/initiative efficiency exchange rate when writing Charms.<br /> <br /> You can spend 2m on an Excellency to raise a static value like DV by 1. By the basic application of Reed, spending 2i increases Evasion by 1. So, in this case, 1 initiative is worth a little more than 1 mote, as activating Reed also raises the cap on your potential DV by your Essence - a potential benefit, but I don't think it's enough to radically alter efficiency for this discussion. Let's call it 1:1.<br /> <br /> Next, HGD isn't just an initiative cost for the damage cancelling effect - it's 4 motes flat cost plus 1 initiative per damage cancelled. Because part of HGD's cost is variable and part is flat, it's impossible to set a simple mote to initiative cost between HGD and VD - VD is 1i cheaper at 1 blocked success, then VD is paying 4 motes for 2i, then 8 motes for 3i, 12 motes for 4i... by those conversions, 1i starts at literally worthless at 1i=0, and attempts to reach 1i to 4m, but will never quite get there because math.<br /> <br /> So, we have 1i=1m, 1i=0, 1i=2m, and 1i is slightly under 4m, derived from looking at just a few Charms. I'm sure we can find other exchange rates given even a little bit of effort, but I think that proves the point.<br /> <br /> In other words, as far as I can tell, there isn't any balanced conversion cost between initiative and motes. Trying to assign one is just going to drive you crazy because you're assuming that sort of thing was being carefully considered during design, but if it was, it isn't really well reflected in the final product.<br /> <br /> Math aside, I'd say that I think Dodge Charms overall should be better. Dodge has always felt underwhelming to me. It's theoretically valuable as a Charm tree that punishes attackers by draining their initiative and sucking it up for your use, but in a game with transparent mechanics where attackers know that's going to happen after they've taken a first swing, most opponents are just going to attack any other available targets and the Dodge Supernal is just going to sit there and not get attacked. If you're focusing on Dodge as your primary combat ability, you definitely still need a good offensive ability that will force your opponent to consider you a threat... that said, this has always been the case in Exalted, so it isn't really anything new.<br /> <br /> At least part of your specific problem at the moment seems to be that HGD is a weird, badly written, badly balanced Charm with too many different benefits for different costs. It's been referred to as &quot;Word Soup&quot; in another now-ancient thread on the subject, and I think there's good reason for that. If you think it's trying to act like 3 different Charms, I'd suggest that the easiest fix would be to cut it up into three different Charms.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw in the Golden Calibration charm rewrite where the author notes that RST and the unexpected attack section in the Combat rules were from different versions of the unexpected attacks rules, clarified by the developers. I think my problem is that I have been away from a lot of these discussions over the years so I'm trying to play catch up. I was very active on the white wolf forums years ago but my 3rd edition discussion-fu is very weak.<br /> <br /> Word Soup is a good way to say it. For my rewrite, I just ported over 7SE into HGD with some minor changes and allowed both to defend against unexpected attacks as they are basically one-use tricks. I figure, if my Melee characters want a damage nullifier, they can just port over VD.<br /> <br /> The initiative to essence conversion explanation was amazing. I'm not the best mather so having someone break it down like that helps a lot. It was elegantly explained. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 01-29-2023, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T08:07:11-08:00","id":1501613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501603#post1501603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me the important question is who's the player character in this situation.<br /> <br /> It's reasonable to say a character can't employ a defensive melee charm when they don't have a melee weapon. It's my opinion that HGD mentioning unexpected attacks was future proofing against magic that gives attacks the properties of an ambush rather than allow a Solar being able to parry an assassin's dagger while asleep in their bed despite their sword being all the way across the room.<br /> <br /> However, people are substantially less reasonable when it's their character on the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, for me, it's more of who invested more into the desired result. If I made a stealth/thrown character heavily invested in both and I do something like Observer-Deceiving Attack into Crimson Razor Wind to get my ambush attack, using 2+ charms and 8+m, 1wp I expect a little more resistance than one charm costing 4m. I know that that is a white room scenario and that defense trumps offense but dodge fairs even worse in this situation. To do the same for dodge, you'd have to spend 5m for RST and still that only works well if the dodger is lucky enough to get back to full Evasion.<br /> <br /> I agree, if the PC is the defender in this scenario, then it is badass to stop an assassin's dagger with HGD. But, if I start paranoia combatting all of my NPCs with HGD effects, then my PC stealth monkey is going to be very put out. My HGD change mentioned in my High Priest reply is probably good enough, at least for my mental well-being, lol.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T17:50:21-08:00","id":1501654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501611#post1501611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw in the Golden Calibration charm rewrite where the author notes that RST and the unexpected attack section in the Combat rules were from different versions of the unexpected attacks rules, clarified by the developers. I think my problem is that I have been away from a lot of these discussions over the years so I'm trying to play catch up. I was very active on the white wolf forums years ago but my 3rd edition discussion-fu is very weak.<br /> <br /> Word Soup is a good way to say it. For my rewrite, I just ported over 7SE into HGD with some minor changes and allowed both to defend against unexpected attacks as they are basically one-use tricks. I figure, if my Melee characters want a damage nullifier, they can just port over VD.<br /> <br /> The initiative to essence conversion explanation was amazing. I'm not the best mather so having someone break it down like that helps a lot. It was elegantly explained. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. Good luck getting the system where you want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T19:33:24-08:00","id":1501842,"title":"","content":"Does HGD reset the attacker to base initiative? My reading is that it does if any damage goes through. It does not if the defender nullifies at the damage. If it always resets the attacker's initiative then that's again straight up better than 7SE. <br /> <br /> Also, why is Adamant Skin Technique complete trash? With heavy art armor and Stam 5, that's only 16 hardness which is not even close to being effective against someone with a join battle enhancer. And even more to that point, why can't it be used against an ambush? Of the three perfects, it should be the MOST likely to work on an ambush, not the least. What's going on with that Charm?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T03:04:26-08:00","id":1501858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501842#post1501842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does HGD reset the attacker to base initiative? My reading is that it does if any damage goes through. It does not if the defender nullifies at the damage. If it always resets the attacker's initiative then that's again straight up better than 7SE.<br /> <br /> Also, why is Adamant Skin Technique complete trash? With heavy art armor and Stam 5, that's only 16 hardness which is not even close to being effective against someone with a join battle enhancer. And even more to that point, why can't it be used against an ambush? Of the three perfects, it should be the MOST likely to work on an ambush, not the least. What's going on with that Charm?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>HGD - A &quot;successful attack&quot; for the purposes of resetting to base is if the attack hit, not whether damage is dealt. It just didn't do any damage. It's the same as if the attacker had hit and rolled no damage. Reset to base.<br /> <br /> 7SE isn't a great comparison for that particular part of the Charm - the more direct comparison here would be VD, which explicitly states that it resets to base when damage is paid off down to 0. Not sure why it states that in one Charm but not the other, but here we are.<br /> <br /> Adamant Skin Technique - This doesn't set hardness. It applies soak to a decisive attack's damage dice - in your example, it removes 16 from their initiative that they don't even get to roll as it has been soaked. And it is compatible with one Charm - Diamond Body Prana, which always results in at least a boost of 3 soak, making your soak a minimum of 19 with the artifact armor and 5 stamina, more likely 22-23 or so assuming your roll isn't terrible.<br /> <br /> This is very good efficiency - with 23 soak and assuming an average roll for the attacker, it removes about 9 successes on a damage roll for 8 motes. Compared to the same effect from VD (36 motes) or HGD (4m9i), this is a steal - and a very serious Solar combatant can then buy off whatever's left with one of those Charms if necessary. Even if you have the 16 soak mentioned above, perhaps because you haven't activated Diamond Body, that's still about 6 average damage removed. And against mortal foes who probably don't have 23/16 initiative banked, will usually will reset them to base with no risk to you.<br /> <br /> A potential problem with it is that unlike 7SE or HGD, it doesn't have the &quot;you can do this after the attack hits&quot; wording, so you unfortunately need to declare it when you think the upcoming attack might be a doozy. If you think you need to activate this, you might be better off declaring that you're intentionally letting yourself get hit, since extra successes don't add damage dice on decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> As for the ambush thing, it's a bummer. I still don't have an answer for you one why HGD and only HGD gets ambush protection built in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T05:36:52-08:00","id":1501865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501842#post1501842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the main mistake you're making is that you're directly comparing HGD, SSE and AST to each other because they're the old perfect defences but the truth of the matter is they've got different strengths and weaknesses along with important synergy with other charms in their tree. <br /> <br /> If I had to tier them based on my experience I'd personally rank them AST &gt; SSE &gt; HGD.<br /> <br /> The main reason for this is that the weakness of the damage absorption part of HGD is being low on initiative which is more likely to come up than the failure conditions of the other two and broadly the melee tree does less to support it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T12:28:25-08:00","id":1501971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501858#post1501858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> HGD - A &quot;successful attack&quot; for the purposes of resetting to base is if the attack hit, not whether damage is dealt. It just didn't do any damage. It's the same as if the attacker had hit and rolled no damage. Reset to base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. Once again, HGD is just a better Charm than 7SE. If someone went out of their way to hit me and I used 7SE, they would lose 3 init and just try again next round and I'm out of 7SE. Someone could go out of their way and hit me with HGD and I just nullify as much of the damage as I can without crashing myself and they are reset to 3. Then I just smack them, crash them, and I'm back to my high initiative and I can do it again next turn. That seems very unfair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501858#post1501858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7SE isn't a great comparison for that particular part of the Charm - the more direct comparison here would be VD, which explicitly states that it resets to base when damage is paid off down to 0. Not sure why it states that in one Charm but not the other, but here we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a lot of those &quot;random rule clarifications&quot; like the one in VD and the one in RST about ambushes and Charms should have been written with a &quot;Just as a reminder.... this rule is still in effect.&quot; Instead, the reader reads it as a specific aspect of that particular Charm when it's supposed to be a universal rule. I also feel that they forgot about the dice caps in most of the auto-success charms. Luckily, in the DB book they mention non-charm successes in the Charm to help with that. The worst culprit of the &quot;I forgot about the dice caps&quot; charm in the core book is definitely Living Shadow Preparedness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501858#post1501858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adamant Skin Technique - This doesn't set hardness. It applies soak to a decisive attack's damage dice - in your example, it removes 16 from their initiative that they don't even get to roll as it has been soaked. And it is compatible with one Charm - Diamond Body Prana, which always results in at least a boost of 3 soak, making your soak a minimum of 19 with the artifact armor and 5 stamina, more likely 22-23 or so assuming your roll isn't terrible.<br /> <br /> This is very good efficiency - with 23 soak and assuming an average roll for the attacker, it removes about 9 successes on a damage roll for 8 motes. Compared to the same effect from VD (36 motes) or HGD (4m9i), this is a steal - and a very serious Solar combatant can then buy off whatever's left with one of those Charms if necessary. Even if you have the 16 soak mentioned above, perhaps because you haven't activated Diamond Body, that's still about 6 average damage removed. And against mortal foes who probably don't have 23/16 initiative banked, will usually will reset them to base with no risk to you.<br /> <br /> A potential problem with it is that unlike 7SE or HGD, it doesn't have the &quot;you can do this after the attack hits&quot; wording, so you unfortunately need to declare it when you think the upcoming attack might be a doozy. If you think you need to activate this, you might be better off declaring that you're intentionally letting yourself get hit, since extra successes don't add damage dice on decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my reading of AST and DBP is that AST says it removes (stam+armor soak) from the decisive attack's dice pool. This is not soak but a random dice roll. So, even though DBP is mentioned, by the wording of the charms DBP does nothing to help because it adds soak to withering attacks and hardness to decisive attacks which in no way aids in the (stam+armor soak) dice removal of AST. If this has been errata'd, then that's not a bad synergy.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;average roll for the attacker.&quot; Do you mean if they had, let's say, 35 initiative versus your 23 (stam+armor soak+DBP), subtracted down to 12 dice and rolled 9 successes? Or, wait, have I been reading AST wrong this whole time and it just acts as your &quot;evasion&quot; for the attack? You'd have 23 resistance &quot;evasion&quot; against the attack dice pool and not the damage dice pool? Is that why Hardness is set to 0?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501858#post1501858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the ambush thing, it's a bummer. I still don't have an answer for you one why HGD and only HGD gets ambush protection built in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the devs meant for &quot;any source&quot; to include ambushes for 7SE but failed to realize that that doesn't beat their own rulings on ambushes.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 02-02-2023, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:01:48-08:00","id":1501976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501971#post1501971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, even though DBP is mentioned, by the wording of the charms DBP does nothing to help because it adds soak to withering attacks and hardness to decisive attacks which in no way aids in the (stam+armor soak) dice removal of AST. If this has been errata'd, then that's not a bad synergy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given how it is explicitly mentioned like that why would you think the idea that it does nothing? The intent and wording seems clear enough. LIke if I write a charm that says &quot;other soak adding charms don't help except for this one&quot; it seems really weird to fixate that my prior wording doesn't quite fit the technical language and not understand that the idea is yeah, the charm I specifically said is the exception actually does help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T14:32:15-08:00","id":1501983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BogMod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501976#post1501976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given how it is explicitly mentioned like that why would you think the idea that it does nothing? The intent and wording seems clear enough. LIke if I write a charm that says &quot;other soak adding charms don't help except for this one&quot; it seems really weird to fixate that my prior wording doesn't quite fit the technical language and not understand that the idea is yeah, the charm I specifically said is the exception actually does help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording of the charm in no way seems clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Channeling Essence through her Resistance, she may apply her full (Stamina + armor soak) to a decisive attack.\u200b </div> </div> </div> This states that the (stamina +armor soak) applies to the attack dice pool. What it should have said was &quot;she may apply her full soak (Stamina + armor soak) to a decisive attack's damage pool.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As this Charm is a counter to decisive attacks, the weapon\u2019s overwhelming damage does not apply without a Charm.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This line makes no sense but let's just assume it's referencing the damage dice pool. Overwhelming is a WITHERING DAMAGE rule, not a decisive damage rule so this is complete trash ruling as this is a decisive-only Charm. If they wrote it as a reminder that Overwhelming doesn't apply to decisive attacks, then okay, but why even include it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This effect is incompatible with Charms that increase soak except for Diamond-Body Prana,\u200b </div> </div> </div>This is not a &quot;soak&quot; charm because it never states that it is. The (stamina +armor soak) DICE POOL could be seen as a soak but it is not actually explained as such and therefore soak Charms do not add to the (stamina +armor soak) dice pool. I agree, it should be INTERPRETED that way but it is not written out correctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adamant Skin Technique can\u2019t be invoked against an ambush attack\u200b </div> </div> </div>This ruling only makes sense if AST is Resistance &quot;evasion&quot; and that you use it to stop the ambush's attack dice pool, not the damage dice pool. If it doesn't work on the attack, but nullifies damage dice, then why wouldn't it work like every other soak/hardness charm? My guess is because of this line<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invoking Adamant Skin Technique sets the Solar\u2019s hardness to 0 for one instant.\u200b </div> </div> </div> which means that the resistance &quot;evasion&quot; of let's say 10-25 is far higher than most PC's Defense score and therefore the balance to that is that if the attack does manage to hit (via ambush or really high rolling) then the user gets smacked with a really hard decisive damage roll.<br /> <br /> I think the IDEA of the charm is that against a decisive damage pool, the AST user gets to subtract their full soak (including buffs from DBP) from an opponent's decisive damage dice pool. But, this charm in no way actually says that. In fact, it's FILLED with bad wording and pointless rulings. I could easily read it either as a dice-subtractor from the attack pool or damage pool. In fact, the more I read it, the less clear I am on what the charm actually does.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T23:43:36-08:00","id":1502011,"title":"","content":"You are overthinking it.<br /> <br /> 2E had Mechanics Keywords. If a Charm said it was Obvious, then it was Obvious. If it was a Crippling Effect, it was a Crippling Effect.<br /> <br /> 3E uses natural language. If a Charm says &quot;this other Charm applies&quot;, then the other Charm applies. Some have reminder text baked in to the wording. Some don't. Some have rules exceptions made explicit in the wording. Some only imply.<br /> <br /> And, like, at your table, your gaming group is free to interpret the rules however you like. Have fun. The only &quot;wrong&quot; way to play the game is the way you don't enjoy.<br /> <br /> But if you want to know the intent on how things work, you can ask the community who has been playing this and asking the devs for clarifications, and we'll tell you.<br /> <br /> Adamant Skin Technique lets you apply your Soak to a Decisive Attack. You can boast your Soak with Diamond-Body Prana.<br /> <br /> Don't over think it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T12:06:50-08:00","id":1502038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502011#post1502011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E uses natural language. If a Charm says &quot;this other Charm applies&quot;, then the other Charm applies. Some have reminder text baked in to the wording. Some don't. Some have rules exceptions made explicit in the wording. Some only imply.</div> </div> </div> </div>What an awful way to run a complex game. It's really not that hard to be exact with your wording. Decisive Attack has TWO different rolls in it. It wouldn't have been hard to write &quot;Decisive Damage roll&quot; instead of &quot;Decisive Attack&quot; especially when word count was CLEARLY not an issue with the tome we received. <br /> <br /> I shouldn't have to go to a forum to figure out the intent of a charm like I'm in a theology class or something. It should just be exactly what it is. Fluff at the top, mechanics at the bottom. The interspersed fluff and mechanics, the redundant reminder text NOT SPELLED OUT LIKE A REMINDER as in &quot;Just as a reminder, this charm still returns the attacker to base initiative&quot; but as a possible exception to the rule, the lack of consistency with really anything, the forgetful dice cap rule in half of the success adder charms, etc etc. drives me crazy and should not exist past a first draft.<br /> <br /> I think my problem with the edition is it's clearly a first draft pawned off like a &quot;developer's choice to be written like this&quot; and I hate it. 3 years in development and this is the final product. Meh.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine if magic cards had the players use the INTENT OF THE WRITER to play? The game would shut down. <br /> <br /> Also, the game developers clearly thought through the charms and the applications of complex play because they do add in parts in AST such as &quot;can't be used in an ambush,&quot; &quot;hardness 0 for an instant&quot;, etc. I don't know why they couldn't go back and clean up their mess of a word vomit after the fact and be more concise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502011#post1502011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you want to know the intent on how things work, you can ask the community who has been playing this and asking the devs for clarifications, and we'll tell you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm not mad at your response. I'm just a bit frustrated with a game I love. Don't take my tone personally. I'm actually quite happy the community is still as helpful as it ever was. Love you guys. I think I just hate John Morke lol.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T14:57:49-08:00","id":1502051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502038#post1502038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What an awful way to run a complex game. It's really not that hard to be exact with your wording. Decisive Attack has TWO different rolls in it. It wouldn't have been hard to write &quot;Decisive Damage roll&quot; instead of &quot;Decisive Attack&quot; especially when word count was CLEARLY not an issue with the tome we received.<br /> <br /> I shouldn't have to go to a forum to figure out the intent of a charm like I'm in a theology class or something. It should just be exactly what it is. Fluff at the top, mechanics at the bottom. The interspersed fluff and mechanics, the redundant reminder text NOT SPELLED OUT LIKE A REMINDER as in &quot;Just as a reminder, this charm still returns the attacker to base initiative&quot; but as a possible exception to the rule, the lack of consistency with really anything, the forgetful dice cap rule in half of the success adder charms, etc etc. drives me crazy and should not exist past a first draft.<br /> <br /> I think my problem with the edition is it's clearly a first draft pawned off like a &quot;developer's choice to be written like this&quot; and I hate it. 3 years in development and this is the final product. Meh.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine if magic cards had the players use the INTENT OF THE WRITER to play? The game would shut down.<br /> <br /> Also, the game developers clearly thought through the charms and the applications of complex play because they do add in parts in AST such as &quot;can't be used in an ambush,&quot; &quot;hardness 0 for an instant&quot;, etc. I don't know why they couldn't go back and clean up their mess of a word vomit after the fact and be more concise.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm not mad at your response. I'm just a bit frustrated with a game I love. Don't take my tone personally. I'm actually quite happy the community is still as helpful as it ever was. Love you guys. I think I just hate John Morke lol.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I wasn't around during the intial KS and development but I know the lead developers changed towards the very end of the development of core. The guys who took over have done all of the other splats and resources and those do not have the issues that core has that are causing you so much trouble. So for the most part this is just an issues with Solars but they are still stronger than the others just not by leaps and bounds like I've heard they were in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T16:08:23-08:00","id":1502060,"title":"","content":"In every edition, Solars have suffered by being the first exalted type, and by being created along the ruleset for the edition. All other Exalted types tended to get better charmsets technology (not necessarily in terms of power), as the system is done, better understood, and better tools and charm technologies are designed.<br /> <br /> 3rd edition is in no way different in this aspect, except even more so. Every other splat Crafts charmset is much better than the solar one (no wonder), but that's true for many other charmsets, such as War and Presence (and Sail and...). Even the combat charmsets, which were considered 'good', are showing their age.<br /> <br /> And it does not stop there: the kickstarted sidereal charmset as a whole is leaps and bounds tighter and more interesting than the solar one (what reminds me of 1st ed, without the non-intentional power creep SMA and unbound successes caused), as it has clear and declared themes per charmset. Even the Abyssal charmset (which used to be in earlier editions just solar-charmset charm per charm, but dark!) seems pretty promising from what I've heard.<br /> <br /> It's a pity there's this 'no retreads' policy in this edition, as the necessity of a redone Solar charmset is pretty obvious to everybody. I lost count of the fan remakes I've seen, but I'd pay a pretty penny for a professionally done solar charmset done by the folks that are working on the newer books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T19:30:58-08:00","id":1502072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501971#post1501971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to know. Once again, HGD is just a better Charm than 7SE. If someone went out of their way to hit me and I used 7SE, they would lose 3 init and just try again next round and I'm out of 7SE. Someone could go out of their way and hit me with HGD and I just nullify as much of the damage as I can without crashing myself and they are reset to 3. Then I just smack them, crash them, and I'm back to my high initiative and I can do it again next turn. That seems very unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can evaluate the Charms based on such a limited range of scenarios when there are a lot of possibilities in this system.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea that an attacker against Seven Shadows Evasion just loses 3 Initiative and can try again is not considering what might have gone into the attack to make it worth perfectly dodging in the first place. It might have cost a lot of motes that don't replenish by their next turn. It might require them to have an Initiative advantage over the opponent that they've lost. It might also be an attack that can only be used once per scene. Meanwhile the Solar, having lost no Initiative, might take the opportunity to respond with a Decisive Attack of their own.<br /> <br /> Your scenario for Heavenly Guardian Defence can be complicated by so much as one additional attacker who might Crash the Solar before they get the chance to Crash the person who reset to base off of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T05:36:47-08:00","id":1502098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502051#post1502051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I wasn't around during the intial KS and development but I know the lead developers changed towards the very end of the development of core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're mixing some things up. Robert Vance and Eric Minton did not become developers until well after the core was released.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T06:17:08-08:00","id":1502099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502051#post1502051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I wasn't around during the intial KS and development but I know the lead developers changed towards the very end of the development of core. The guys who took over have done all of the other splats and resources and those do not have the issues that core has that are causing you so much trouble. So for the most part this is just an issues with Solars but they are still stronger than the others just not by leaps and bounds like I've heard they were in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've read through the DB charmset now trying to get a feel for where the Solar charms sit and, in general, the charms are more concise and to the point. It really is just loose, unedited word vomit in the corebook. Oh well, it's to be expected at this point. Maybe 4th edition will start with Exigents and we'll get Solars as the 4th splat and have a good solar charmset for once.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:16:50-08:00","id":1502154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502060#post1502060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In every edition, Solars have suffered by being the first exalted type, and by being created along the ruleset for the edition. All other Exalted types tended to get better charmsets technology (not necessarily in terms of power), as the system is done, better understood, and better tools and charm technologies are designed.<br /> <br /> 3rd edition is in no way different in this aspect, except even more so. Every other splat Crafts charmset is much better than the solar one (no wonder), but that's true for many other charmsets, such as War and Presence (and Sail and...). Even the combat charmsets, which were considered 'good', are showing their age.<br /> <br /> And it does not stop there: the kickstarted sidereal charmset as a whole is leaps and bounds tighter and more interesting than the solar one (what reminds me of 1st ed, without the non-intentional power creep SMA and unbound successes caused), as it has clear and declared themes per charmset. Even the Abyssal charmset (which used to be in earlier editions just solar-charmset charm per charm, but dark!) seems pretty promising from what I've heard.<br /> <br /> <b>It's a pity there's this 'no retreads' policy in this edition, as the necessity of a redone Solar charmset is pretty obvious to everybody. I lost count of the fan remakes I've seen, but <u>I'd pay a pretty penny for a professionally done solar charmset done by the folks that are working on the newer books.</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, a lot of people would <i>not </i>and would in fact be pretty mad if they were asked to pay for the privilege of receiving errata on a charm set that isn't up to snuff with the quality the rest of the line has. Why should Paradox/Onyx Path get our money twice for fixing a mistake <i>they </i>made in the original product? I'm not going to double dip and pay them twice for the same product, I am not made of money and able to just throw wads of cash away on my entertainment products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T02:54:15-08:00","id":1502187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501971#post1501971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to know. Once again, HGD is just a better Charm than 7SE. If someone went out of their way to hit me and I used 7SE, they would lose 3 init and just try again next round and I'm out of 7SE. Someone could go out of their way and hit me with HGD and I just nullify as much of the damage as I can without crashing myself and they are reset to 3. Then I just smack them, crash them, and I'm back to my high initiative and I can do it again next turn. That seems very unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> And as mentioned before, the idea of nullifying &quot;as much of the damage as you can without crashing&quot; is that this might be 2 if you just reset to base. 7SE is just &quot;nope you missed&quot;, even if you're low on initiative. Since defenders declare Charms after attackers and 3E does system transparency, you can do this after hearing that they're activating 4 different Charms and spending 20ish motes - an attack you probably want to avoid for 4 motes 1 willpower rather than risking that they're about to roll a massive pile of damage that your 3 initiative probably won't be able to buy off.<br /> <br /> They fill different roles, and one or the other is better in different situations. Again, I think the main comparison here should be between VD and HGD, not 7SE unless you're talking about the uncountable environmental damage function that both 7SE and HGD cover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1501971#post1501971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;average roll for the attacker.&quot; Do you mean if they had, let's say, 35 initiative versus your 23 (stam+armor soak+DBP), subtracted down to 12 dice and rolled 9 successes? Or, wait, have I been reading AST wrong this whole time and it just acts as your &quot;evasion&quot; for the attack? You'd have 23 resistance &quot;evasion&quot; against the attack dice pool and not the damage dice pool? Is that why Hardness is set to 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers I listed are the statistically probable number of health levels that a given amount of dice in a decisive attack would likely do. You're likely to end up with 40% of your damage dice resulting in successes - you might roll high, you might roll low, but when you're thinking how many you'll probably get, 40% is the number to guesstimate. For the 23 example, removing 23 initiative before you roll would be 9 probable damage successes.<br /> <br /> Hardness is set to 0 to indicate that you can't use AST to soak and then apply hardness afterwards - if you activate AST, you get soak instead of hardness, which is better.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that threw you off, I could have explained it better.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of your post, it sounds like a lot of it has already been clarified - AST is soak, but for decisive damage pools (ie, initiative) instead of withering. DBP successes count for this, but not other soak Charms. It's not written particularly clearly, as the main intent when writing Charms for 3E Solars didn't include clarity as a primary concern, instead prioritizing whatever the designer felt sounds good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 02-05-2023, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T06:06:52-08:00","id":1502199,"title":"","content":"Plus, like... however Dodge's defensive capacity measures up against that of Melee, it's still going to be your best bet if you don't fight with a sword.<br /> <br /> I think some of the argument that Charms to aid Parry are lacking some nuances, but I'd also say that even if after all of that Melee could be objectively measured to come out a bit ahead that's not a terrible thing if Melee requires the buy-in of defining what kind of weapon you can fight with to access that form of defence, and that if the Dodge options were enhanced then it might undermine the value of ever parrying in the first place.<br /> <br /> And thus Heavenly Guardian Defence isn't just a matter of comparing defensive options but comparing entire combat Abilities. That Melee is good in an all-around way is part of what sets it apart from Archery, Brawl and Throne, each of which has its own merits that one may prefer over what Melee offers but includes the element of Dodge being a lot more helpful for rounding out one's defence. Not totally necessary, mind, Brawl still has a bit of power for getting by on that front and Archery and Thrown can circumstantially benefit without much Defence if one is attacking a target that is out of range for reprisal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T14:06:20-08:00","id":1503162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502154#post1502154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, a lot of people would <i>not </i>and would in fact be pretty mad if they were asked to pay for the privilege of receiving errata on a charm set that isn't up to snuff with the quality the rest of the line has. Why should Paradox/Onyx Path get our money twice for fixing a mistake <i>they </i>made in the original product? I'm not going to double dip and pay them twice for the same product, I am not made of money and able to just throw wads of cash away on my entertainment products.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the solar charmset is not up to par has much to do with the fact that it was developed along the system, and that it was the prototype for other charmsets. Incompatibilities were created, and systemic exploits were underdeveloped. It's still the best solar charm set compared to the other editions, IMO. <br /> <br /> As long as we agree that the solar charms need a refresh and that OP won't publish it for free, you're welcome not to buy it on principles. You can expect them to change their business practices, or wait for a new edition and then buy everything all over again (solar charmset will probably not be perfect, though).<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that it would be much more fun for me to have such a vision. I don't have an issue with the developers being paid for doing so (as I want it to be well done), so I would pay for a revised solar charmset (as I've done in 2nd ed), and I suppose a lot of other players would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T06:09:02-08:00","id":1503376,"title":"","content":"2.5 was free.<br /> Wizards of the Coast errata their games for free.<br /> Piazo errata's for free.<br /> Fantasy Flight errata's for free AND overhauled their flagship RPG with a new corebook v1.5 that fixed most of the buggy crap.<br /> <br /> &quot;Onyx Path won't errata for free!&quot;<br /> <br /> Why not? They should. It's literally the industry standard, and if they polished the game with a 3.5 release (paid to play or free), they would have more customers because they would have a better product.<br /> <br /> Not providing errata is a bad business model because Jack T hates money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T23:50:34-08:00","id":1503429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1503376#post1503376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.5 was free.<br /> Wizards of the Coast errata their games for free.<br /> Piazo errata's for free.<br /> Fantasy Flight errata's for free AND overhauled their flagship RPG with a new corebook v1.5 that fixed most of the buggy crap.<br /> <br /> &quot;Onyx Path won't errata for free!&quot;<br /> <br /> Why not? They should. It's literally the industry standard, and if they polished the game with a 3.5 release (paid to play or free), they would have more customers because they would have a better product.<br /> <br /> Not providing errata is a bad business model because Jack T hates money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because errata is writing and OPP doesn't, when possible, make authors write for free. That WotC doesn't charge us for it doens't mean it's not charged by authors to do so, and has entire budget for R&amp;D.<br /> <br /> 2.5e did it more or less unpaid until DotFA's errata, which note, you had to pay for the PDF due to how extensive the Solar errata was. Arguably, the amount of time-to-hours put in is considered something current writers and devs are straight-up unwilling to do without getting paid for it.<br /> <br /> Fantasy Flight is like WotC. It's a big company that honeslty probably can get away with it due to more folks on salary, rather htan most writers being freelance and again, paid by the word. LIke, take the overhaul fo the corebook. That required paying someon for layout. If not, they ripped someone off.<br /> <br /> Simply put, errata is something that requires someone be giving their time. OPP doens't want folks working for it giving htier time for free. That other companies don't charge means the costs are offset elsewhere...or they are in effect taking from authors, which for companies like WotC or Fantasy Flight, woudl surprise no one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T02:40:06-08:00","id":1503517,"title":"","content":"So pay them?<br /> <br /> The owners of Exalted are worth $2 <i>billion</i>. Billion. With a &quot;b&quot;.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 4th reprinted their corebooks halfway through the line, charged full price, and made a mint. D&amp;D 3.5 was their flagship product before that, and probably the most iconic RPG ever.<br /> <br /> Soft errata in the form of ST guides, and AT8D retconning the corebook, and kickstarter add ons not needing the MA merit, and Arms just straight printing errata, and Exigients telling you how Charms work, and the devs spending hours engaging with the community and talking about the game... is already there.<br /> <br /> Exalted would sell more copies and make more money with Errata.<br /> <br /> Paying writers for their work is an investment that will generate revenue.<br /> <br /> And with how long books spend in layout and how long it takes new books to be approved, and how OPP has brought on new devs for Exalted, the talking points <i>just don't make sense</i>.<br /> <br /> There is <i>no</i> small indie company that doesn't do Errata.<br /> <br /> Brutal Games does errata.<br /> Arc Dream Publishing does errata.<br /> Sine Nomine Publishing does errata.<br /> Green Ronin Publishing does errata.<br /> Modiphius Entertainment does errata.<br /> Dungeons The Dragoning got errata.<br /> <br /> I know what the party line is. I've had conversations with the devs, where they have told me that they don't do errata because they are working on new books. I don't need to be told that folks should be compensated for their labor.<br /> <br /> I am saying that the business decision to not invest in making the game playable, is short-sighted and profit limiting. It is not, by any stretch, standard practice in the industry. OPP is a weird outlier whose weird policy is hurting its bottom line.<br /> <br /> If you can give me one, <i>one</i> other publisher that does not update its games, I will shut up and never mention errata on these forums again.<br /> <br /> But I have a deluxe corebook. I have a POD corebook. I have a pdf corebook.<br /> <br /> I would pay full price for a 3.5 corebook. Exalted Essence <i>triple</i> funded day one of its Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> People <i>want to buy</i> a version of Exalted they can play.<br /> <br /> We love Exalted!<br /> <br /> Please take our money!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-20-2023, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T04:49:51-08:00","id":1503518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1503517#post1503517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The owners of Exalted are worth $2 <i>billion</i>. Billion. With a &quot;b&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's your problem.<br /> <br /> Paradox does not give a shit. They're not giving Onyx Path a cent to help make Exalted better. Exalted exists to generate passive income for Paradox to make the big red hole in their ledgers look less bad as they've failed to capitalize on their purchase of some of the old WW IPs.<br /> <br /> If Paradox thought Exalted was going to cost them more money (even if less than what Onyx Path pays them to make books anyway), they'd just do what they're doing to Chronicles of Darkness and stop approving books to let it die. Even if it would be a smart investment that would make them even more money in the long run. Killing the CofD is costing them money since they can't get licensing fees for books that don't exist.<br /> <br /> Scion 2e got a free errata doc.. but Onyx Path owns Scion completely.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path is an outlier because their position is an outlier. Pretty much every example you're pointing to are companies that own the IPs they're working on, or haven't had their licensing partner just stop refusing to let them make books that were profitable for both sides because those books aren't the IP owner's pet favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T05:05:22-08:00","id":1503519,"title":"","content":"2nd edition ended up getting extensive errata to the various Charmsets, but that was only after all of the splats were done being printed. In general it's simply going to be viewed as a better business decision to write new material for people to use, than to revamp old material for free. I mean personally, I'd much rather see Abyssals finally get printed rather than have them be put off for another year or two because the authors went back to do rewrites of older Charmsets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-21-2023, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T21:35:29-08:00","id":1503599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1502154#post1502154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, a lot of people would <i>not </i>and would in fact be pretty mad if they were asked to pay for the privilege of receiving errata on a charm set that isn't up to snuff with the quality the rest of the line has. Why should Paradox/Onyx Path get our money twice for fixing a mistake <i>they </i>made in the original product? I'm not going to double dip and pay them twice for the same product, I am not made of money and able to just throw wads of cash away on my entertainment products.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Scroll of Errata in 2nd edition free?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T22:54:11-08:00","id":1503600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1503599#post1503599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't the Scroll of Errata in 2nd edition free?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also something writers have noted was thousands of words, and something they put a lot of time in. It was volunteer work. Hell, laying it out was volunteer work also. It was mostly a fan effort that was allowed since it was free. The same authors have since noted that it was a lot of time and man hours on something they didn't get paid for.<br /> <br /> There's also a good chunk of htings that weren't free, like the updated <i>Dreams of the First Age</i>, which was basically a new PDF/PoD purchase.<br /> <br /> Some of the other publishers kind of are also not quite teh same thing. Sine Nomine was mentioend but that's literally one person, doing most all the work and more or less not contracting anyone. Versus a company which seems to not want to have authors do work for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T23:08:25-08:00","id":1503666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1503518#post1503518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion 2e got a free errata doc.. but Onyx Path owns Scion completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion is a bad example for this because there wouldn't be an errata doc for it either if the wrong file hadn't been sent to print. If it hadn't been glaringly obvious that the final printed product backers got was a near-completion draft, it wouldn't exist.<br /> <br /> Even then, the product still has significant issues that could be easily addressed by another update of the errata doc. It's definitely a case of Onyx Path doing the absolute minimum in an attempt to placate backers, not an example of them making good on supporting a product.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path generally doesn't do errata or other post-release support. That's pretty obviously their policy. I don't think Paradox is doing a great job as the IP holder of most of the old White Wolf stuff, but they aren't the source of the current policy of neglecting the widespread industry standard of basic errata documents. Frankly, I don't think Paradox cares enough to bother declaring &quot;No errata!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T23:55:47-08:00","id":1503667,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the industry standard of issuing errata looks a lot more like Scion 2e's one (aka a few pages with of single line corrections that only covers very specific mistakes and doesn't get into large in-depth changes) not &quot;redo the whole Solar Charm set for free.&quot;<br /> <br /> All those free errata that are &quot;industry standard&quot; are just as unsatisfactory to most of those games' fans as Onyx Path's &quot;we get what we get during the backer edit/feedback cycle,&quot; because like Scion 2e's one, they're generally never going to cover a lot of things that actually require thought and deliberation from the designers over spelling errors/word swaps/stat block fixes/etc.<br /> <br /> Paizo once had four such errata for the same book (though it should be noted each was released before a new print edition was being released, so it was basically just a free change-log for fixes in the new print run), and still ended up with a very substantial FAQ thread on their forums for all the stuff those little corrections didn't cover The &quot;everyone else does free errata&quot; looks way more like what Onyx Path does in end result than it looks like what Exalted 2e got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T10:17:01-08:00","id":1503951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1503519#post1503519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean personally, I'd much rather see Abyssals finally get printed rather than have them be put off for another year or two because the authors went back to do rewrites of older Charmsets.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd really rather have playable Abyssals than playable Solars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T12:14:07-08:00","id":1503959,"title":"","content":"I think a detailed fix to the Solar charmset would benefit from seeing Abyssals and/or Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T10:00:19-08:00","id":1504602,"title":"","content":"Hi Guys,<br /> <br /> I see this thread has taken on a new direction, which is fine but I'd like to ask a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> First, it would seem that some of the balancing points to HGD was that it was Decisive-only but it would appear that that was errata'd out, at least the unexpected part of it. Do you think that is a good errata or did you think the limiting factor of only being able to block unexpected attacks if they are decisive is a good balance to dodge charms?<br /> <br /> Second, my player wants to know if he has to pay for Thunderbolt Attack Prana comboed with Iron Whirlwind Attack for each attack or is it just paid for once like Hungry Tiger Technique?<br /> <br /> Third, can someone explain to me why Shower of Deadly Blades costs 6m, 1wp. It seems EXTREMELY underpowered for the cost and requirements. Am I just reading it incorrectly? How can 2 initiative per target that isn't the original target be worth all that? How does it &quot;scatter&quot; groups when the most it can do to a battle group is drop it by 2 initiative? Why does it warrant an ammunition check? All these downsides for 2 initiative that the Solar doesn't receive. Am I missing the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 03-06-2023, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T14:39:46-08:00","id":1504648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504602#post1504602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Guys,<br /> <br /> I see this thread has taken on a new direction, which is fine but I'd like to ask a couple of questions:<br /> <br /> First, it would seem that some of the balancing points to HGD was that it was Decisive-only but it would appear that that was errata'd out, at least the unexpected part of it. Do you think that is a good errata or did you think the limiting factor of only being able to block unexpected attacks if they are decisive is a good balance to dodge charms?<br /> <br /> Second, my player wants to know if he has to pay for Thunderbolt Attack Prana comboed with Iron Whirlwind Attack for each attack or is it just paid for once like Hungry Tiger Technique?<br /> <br /> Third, can someone explain to me why Shower of Deadly Blades costs 6m, 1wp. It seems EXTREMELY underpowered for the cost and requirements. Am I just reading it incorrectly? How can 2 initiative per target that isn't the original target be worth all that? How does it &quot;scatter&quot; groups when the most it can do to a battle group is drop it by 2 initiative? Why does it warrant an ammunition check? All these downsides for 2 initiative that the Solar doesn't receive. Am I missing the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. As far as I know, it wasn't errata'd out. The Decisive-only tag is still present, and I don't see anything about withering ambush attacks being an exception to the tag in the text of the Charm. Decisive attacks only.<br /> <br /> 2. I would say that Thunderbolt Attack Prana is an &quot;attack-enhancing Charm&quot;, so only pay for it once.<br /> <br /> 3. I tend to agree that Shower of Deadly Blades is pretty weak for the cost. It's also poorly written - not given any consideration for Artifact throwing weapons, not giving any actual thought toward how it would interact with battle groups despite the fluff text indicating that's a big part of its purpose.<br /> <br /> Two things you have wrong - first, it will scale from 1 to 5 initiative, based mostly on Essence. That can be a significant amount coming from a high Essence character, who could theoretically drop a cluster of foes into initiative crash. Whether the crash bonus would be awarded to the Solar is less clear-cut, though I'd argue that the intent of the charm seems to lean toward no.<br /> <br /> Second, it wouldn't drop the battle group's initiative, as battle groups have inert initiative. I would argue that a battle group should take some amount of magnitude damage instead, but it doesn't have any actual rules included for how much and the normal rules uses pre-rolled initiative dice. Personally, I would say it does magnitude equal to initiative it would deal to a normal character, so 1-5. Half that rounded up would be a more conservative conversion. I would also say that if it prompted a rout check, it would include the +1 difficulty modifier as a supernatural area-of-affect attack.<br /> <br /> I suppose it could also be used to apply some Supplemental Thrown effects on a group of clustered enemies, but at a cursory glance I'm not seeing a lot of withering supplemental thrown charms that would apply well here.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to address the ammunition checks, as I don't like those rules at all - they just serve to serve as an annoyance to ranged combat characters, who then get to have the &quot;fun&quot; of sitting out for a combat for a round or two doing trivial scavenging rolls.<br /> <br /> I still don't think that it's great for the cost, especially at low Essence, unless I'm also missing some sort of point.<br /> <br /> You may or may not also try reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886029-battle-groups-and-aoe-effects\">This Thread</a>, in which people were talking about area of effect attacks and battle groups in general for a wider range of opinions on the topic. Unfortunately it breaks down pretty quickly, as the rules aren't great on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:30:37-08:00","id":1504660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. As far as I know, it wasn't errata'd out. The Decisive-only tag is still present, and I don't see anything about withering ambush attacks being an exception to the tag in the text of the Charm. Decisive attacks only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance clarified it in the &quot;unofficial dev errata&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I would say that Thunderbolt Attack Prana is an &quot;attack-enhancing Charm&quot;, so only pay for it once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that's too powerful?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I tend to agree that Shower of Deadly Blades is pretty weak for the cost. It's also poorly written - not given any consideration for Artifact throwing weapons, not giving any actual thought toward how it would interact with battle groups despite the fluff text indicating that's a big part of its purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things you have wrong - first, it will scale from 1 to 5 initiative, based mostly on Essence. That can be a significant amount coming from a high Essence character, who could theoretically drop a cluster of foes into initiative crash. Whether the crash bonus would be awarded to the Solar is less clear-cut, though I'd argue that the intent of the charm seems to lean toward no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just going off the base level of the power as it's prereq is Essence 2. Even at Essence 5, though, it seems pretty meh. I think the intent was also no. &quot;Indirectly crashing&quot; opponents is a storyteller determined issue RAW but I think it should apply to dodge charms that steal initiative and maybe this charm as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, it wouldn't drop the battle group's initiative, as battle groups have inert initiative. I would argue that a battle group should take some amount of magnitude damage instead, but it doesn't have any actual rules included for how much and the normal rules uses pre-rolled initiative dice. Personally, I would say it does magnitude equal to initiative it would deal to a normal character, so 1-5. Half that rounded up would be a more conservative conversion. I would also say that if it prompted a rout check, it would include the +1 difficulty modifier as a supernatural area-of-affect attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my initial reading of it but then I remembered it didn't actually say it did magnitude damage to groups so I edited my post to say initiative 'damage' to battle groups. I think charms like Searing Quicksilver Flight SHOULD take away initiative to battle groups. My reading is that their 'inert initiative' is solely mentioned for their withering attack damage, not that they can't have it altered by any means. Therefore, I thought that this charm might be useful in lowering their initiative and therefore making them 'scattered' by making them go later in the round. Scattered could and should probably mean magnitude damage though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to address the ammunition checks, as I don't like those rules at all - they just serve to serve as an annoyance to ranged combat characters, who then get to have the &quot;fun&quot; of sitting out for a combat for a round or two doing trivial scavenging rolls.<br /> <br /> I still don't think that it's great for the cost, especially at low Essence, unless I'm also missing some sort of point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504648#post1504648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may or may not also try reading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886029-battle-groups-and-aoe-effects\">This Thread</a>, in which people were talking about area of effect attacks and battle groups in general for a wider range of opinions on the topic. Unfortunately it breaks down pretty quickly, as the rules aren't great on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll check it out, thank you!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T21:42:26-08:00","id":1504812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504660#post1504660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance clarified it in the &quot;unofficial dev errata&quot; thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. I don't personally use the unofficial stuff because if it was actually important, someone on the dev team surely would have made an actual errata pdf in the last 7ish years Exalted has been out.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504660#post1504660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that's too powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's strong, but considering how Iron Whirlwind Attack already splits up your initiative into very small pools, I don't think doubling any that succeed is too strong. For what it costs, Fire and Stones potentially quadrupling your initiative pool by transferring successes into the raw damage pools might actually be more effective.<br /> <br /> The weird part about Thunderbolt would be if you get the extra movement between each attack, which I don't think you should - you're consuming your reflexive movement in the first action, and Iron Whirlwind only gives free cost to attack enhancing Charms, not to movement Charms. But it's such a weird interaction that the whole thing needs to come down to &quot;GMs Call&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504660#post1504660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my initial reading of it but then I remembered it didn't actually say it did magnitude damage to groups so I edited my post to say initiative 'damage' to battle groups. I think charms like Searing Quicksilver Flight SHOULD take away initiative to battle groups. My reading is that their 'inert initiative' is solely mentioned for their withering attack damage, not that they can't have it altered by any means. Therefore, I thought that this charm might be useful in lowering their initiative and therefore making them 'scattered' by making them go later in the round. Scattered could and should probably mean magnitude damage though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using the unofficial dev errata stuff, nothing can change battle group initiative unless it specifically says that it changes battle group initiative EXCEPT that they can voluntarily pay for gambits with initiative costs. I believe Searing Quicksilver is actually the specific Charm that was called out as NOT affecting battle group initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T14:38:35-08:00","id":1504977,"title":"","content":"Edit: Double Post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-14-2023, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T16:07:50-07:00","id":1506186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1501066-long-time-player-new-to-exalted-3rd-edition?p=1504812#post1504812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. I don't personally use the unofficial stuff because if it was actually important, someone on the dev team surely would have made an actual errata pdf in the last 7ish years Exalted has been out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think that, but there has been a consistent anti-errata stance across 3rd edition so far. There has been speculation that this is because Onyx Path don't want to devalue deluxe editions (I've seen this spoken, but never seen it properly sourced, so can't speak as to its truth), but we do have this Discord post made by Eric Minton on the subject in 2020, explaining the stance from another angle:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing proper errata (rather than just giving off-the-cuff recommendations as we currently do) takes a lot of time and energy that would have to be taken away from other work. It would basically be an entire additional book of solid mechanics, which would pretty much bottleneck Vance from developing additional splatbooks for the duration. And either Onyx Path would have to charge for it, which everyone would hate, or they'd have to budget for us to do a book for free, which isn't feasible on the industry's shoestring budgets. And of course it couldn't be printed, because it would need to be updated every time a new book came out or every time someone spotted an inconsistency in an older book that had slipped past folks.<br /> <br /> The old 2e errata was basically a fan project by the old devs. We simply cannot do that on top of our current workloads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that position, I think it's unlikely that we'll get an official errata of any kind for Ex3. Crucible of Legends will have additional rules that can be used, but will not overhaul existing systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T21:24:18-07:00","id":1507095,"title":"","content":"I had the same issues with the system, to the point where I had to rewrite the entity of the Solar charmset from the ground up. Just know you're not alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}